    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27373" root="طول" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسْتَطِيلٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَوِيلٌ</span>. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الفَجْرُ المُسْتَطِيلُ</span> is <i>The
first dawn;</i> also called <i>the false;</i> and termed
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَنَبُ السِّرْحَانِ</span> [the <i>tail of the wolf</i>], because <i>it
appears rising without extending laterally:</i> (Msb:)
opposed to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُسْتَطِيرُ</span>. (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طير</span>.)

